('c4-q34', 4, 34, null, 'Which one of the following will a "ready-aim-fire" culture tend to do with plans for building a new factory?', '["carefully study the plans before building", "get the building process underway before the plans are finished in order to avoid possible objections to expansion", "briefly study the plans before building", "carry out the planning and building process simultaneously to make sure that the plans are updated continuously"]'::jsonb, 'A', null, 'Not marked on the sheet. "Ready-aim-fire" = analyze extensively before committing (vs. "ready-fire-aim" = act first, adjust later).'),
('c4-q35', 4, 35, null, 'Which company would be best suited to a "ready-aim-fire" culture?', '["a chocolate bar company that has made the same successful products for decades", "a pharmaceutical company that is searching for a new way to prevent obesity", "a cell phone company that is seeking to gain market share", "a camera company that is worried that cell phones are taking over its business"]'::jsonb, 'A', 'A', null),
('c4-q36', 4, 36, null, 'Which company would be best suited to a "ready-fire-aim" culture?', '["a chocolate bar company that has made the same successful products for decades", "a pharmaceutical company that is searching for a new way to prevent obesity", "a cell phone company that is seeking to gain market share", "a camera company that is worried that cell phones are taking over its business"]'::jsonb, 'C', null, 'Not marked on the sheet. A fast-moving, highly competitive market (fighting for market share) rewards acting quickly and adjusting later. Somewhat debatable – please double-check with your instructor.'),
